From 85b3df2ee44c1b4b268a1d35c62be973f750fe3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kenan=20Kasumovi=C4=87?=
 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:18:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(launcher): build the game on the device from the
 player's disc

A Linux launcher that needs no generated code (MM3_LAUNCHER_ONLY):
mm3-launcher shows a setup over the settings until the game is built for
it. The player picks a disc image (found in the home folder and on SD
cards, or chosen with the desktop's file dialog), confirms they own it,
and setup/mm3_setup.py beside the launcher checks the disc, copies its
files, translates the code and compiles the game in
~/.local/share/MidtownMadness3, reporting its steps on standard output.
Once built, the footer adds Add to Steam and Rebuild, and Play runs the
start script the setup writes, which is also what Steam and the desktop
menu start. The setup also offers launcher updates from the releases.

The start script sets MM3_LAUNCHER_SKIP: the game's own launcher then
exports the saved settings without opening a window. On arm64 the
settings default to fullscreen at the screen's resolution, 2x MSAA and 2x
detail distance, for a handheld.
